A type that has infinitely many inhabitants (like nat, string, or list), as opposed to finite types like bool or enums with fixed members.

A **type** that has infinitely many inhabitants (like `nat`, `string`, or `list`), as opposed to ${fref("programming-language-theory/concepts/finite-type.td")}s like `bool` or enums with fixed members.
